        "text_RaGXca": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>The  2026 Fall Portfolio features works from Gordon Smith, Amelia Butcher, Marlene Yuen and Arnold Shives. These works have been brought together to consider the idea of place as both a physical environment and a lived experience. Across painting, printmaking, ceramics, and drawing, each artist approaches place as something shaped through memory, community, material, and observation. Their works reveal how landscapes, objects, and histories become vessels for connection, inviting us to reflect on the ways we come to know ourselves, one another, and the environments we inhabit.</p>",
